      "id": 225812,
      "name": "Chaosmancer",
      "username": "Chaosmancer",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/chaosmancer/{size}/1977_2.png",
      "created_at": "2019-03-01T03:52:20.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I could see Mantra (new name for Mr. Fixer) having the Principle of The Mentor.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Also, I could see him having a different named version for the Principle of Clockwork. Clockwork doesn't fit with what he is all about, but I could see him having a principle on the order of things and understanding how that order is created and disrupted.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Honestly, I think the harder part is figuring out what mechanics we will call them, there are some easy things in figuring out what is important to the character.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Also, Expat totally has Principle of the Tactician, she clearly prepared for this and that's why she planted a rifle with special ammo in this warehouse two years ago.</p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:59:33.016Z",
