    {
      "id": 225821,
      "name": "degausser",
      "username": "degausser",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/9fc29f/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2019-03-25T05:51:39.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Just for fun: Principles of the villains-turned-heroes.&nbsp; Again, these are just my guesses off of an incomplete list.</p>\n<p>Luminary: Principle of Ambition, Principle of the Gearhead.</p>\n<p>Lifeline: Principle of Exorcism, Principle of . . . space?</p>\n<p>Akash'Thrya: Principle of Great power, Principle of the team (in a \"All living creatures working together\" sort of way.)</p>\n<p>La Camadora: Principle of the Time Traveler, Principle of the tactician.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Aaaaaaand the Southwest Sentinels.&nbsp; (Note, I said southwest Sentinels, Voidguard would probably have a few differences.)</p>\n<p>Dr. Medico: Principle of healing, Principle of (Element-Healing energy)</p>\n<p>Mainstay: Principle of Stength, Principle of the team</p>\n<p>Idealist: Principle of Levity, Principle of Mastery</p>\n<p>Writhe: Principle of the Gearhead, Principle of (Element-Shadow)</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Anyone who has any other ideas, or would like to voice their own opinions is free to chime in, as long as you are civil.</p>",
      "post_number": 12,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:59:33.639Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
