      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>Just for fun: Principles of the villains-turned-heroes.&nbsp; Again, these are just my guesses off of an incomplete list.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Luminary: Principle of Ambition, Principle of the Gearhead.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Lifeline: Principle of Exorcism, Principle of . . . space?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Akash'Thrya: Principle of Great power, Principle of the team (in a \"All living creatures working together\" sort of way.)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>La Camadora: Principle of the Time Traveler, Principle of the tactician.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Aaaaaaand the Southwest Sentinels.&nbsp; (Note, I said southwest Sentinels, Voidguard would probably have a few differences.)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Dr. Medico: Principle of healing, Principle of (Element-Healing energy)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Mainstay: Principle of Stength, Principle of the team</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Idealist: Principle of Levity, Principle of Mastery</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Writhe: Principle of the Gearhead, Principle of (Element-Shadow)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Anyone who has any other ideas, or would like to voice their own opinions is free to chime in, as long as you are civil.</p>",
